{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK4XPJ1urRmPanjedcNJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`models.FilePathField` now accepts a callable for `path`. I haven't run any tests or tried it against a real model.\n\nThe change is in `FilePathField.formfield()` in `django/db/models/fields/__init__.py`. It calls `path` when it's callable and passes the result to the form field. `deconstruct()` already stores whatever was given, so a callable is written into migrations as the callable itself. The migration then no longer bakes in the path from the machine that ran `makemigrations`.\n\nI didn't touch `forms.FilePathField`, so passing a callable directly to the form field still doesn't work. I also didn't add docs.\n\nFor the case in the issue, you'd define a function that returns `os.path.join(settings.LOCAL_FILE_DIR, 'example_dir')` and pass it as `path=`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":731,"cache_read_input_tokens":19438,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":731},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3bfef74-3d1b-486a-88df-1e65222815c7","uuid":"5ad266e5-9cad-4e37-8f50-59d15fd9fe82","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:21:17.622Z","request_id":"req_011ChK4XP8b5okCk4nF8XPZo"}
